arguments.user_message_template:
Shot: {{shot}}
Actors: {{actors | default("every actor with keys in the chart")}}
Production root: {{output_root}}
Timing chart:
{{context | default("Read the motion step's chart from chain history (v3/charts/<shot>.json); a missing chart is BLOCKED.")}}

Read `v3/creative-spec.md` (D65–D72, Craft baseline, clean-up standard), `v3/rubric.md` (C20–C23) and each actor's `assets/<actor>/model.json`; an actor with no approved model sheet is BLOCKED (run showcase_model_sheet). For each actor generate ONE key sheet through the `imagegen` tool (`tool:imagegen`): `references` are the absolute paths of the actor's model sheet, the approved pick and the shot's card files; the `prompt` lists every key from the chart in order (K1…Kn: pose in words, line of action, what changes) and asks for all of them as full figures on one plate at the model sheet's scale and baseline, numbered left to right, pure black field, five flat colors with identity pigments by hex, pale contour, clean-up standard; `out` is `out/<shot>-keys-<actor>-<NN>.png`. Then, per key: overlay it on the model sheet and report head count and limb ratios (C20, reject above 5 %); fill its silhouette black and judge whether the pose reads (C21); measure contour weight, taper and closure (C22). A rejected key is regenerated once on its own plate with the failing property named in the prompt; a second failure stays REJECTED on the sheet for the owner. Cut every accepted key into `assets/<actor>/keys/<shot>/K<n>.png` with `scripts/cutout.py --field black` (role quantization, soft alpha and contour per D71) and record sha256. If the skeleton toolchain of `v3/studies/tech-rig-01.md` is installed, run it on each key plate and save `K<n>.skeleton.yaml`; otherwise mark joints UNPROVEN, never estimate them by hand. No key is ever tweened by generation (D68). Lay the sheet, overlays and silhouettes into the `KeySheet` composition and render one still.

Return: Keys (actor, id, frame, line of action, plate path, sha256, joints registered yes/no); Model-sheet Overlay (per key); Silhouettes; Clean-up Measured; Sheet Path; Generation Receipts; Rejected Keys; Concerns.
